math","schema":"statement-map-web/2","section":1,"section_title":"Introduction","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:6c2246d27c61a45a1b18c52164bc74ecd19dd7d989ef82442b6e5f594763e5bd","file":"preprints/Nonuniqueness-for-Bounded-Measurable-Scalar-Conductivities-in-Three-Dimensions-September-23-2026/build/paper.tex","line":98,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"5e75c44bfd23d826dd15b966f6b7fd0fa8aa281c6ef618b433aec3998d9ffe22","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Nonuniqueness-for-Bounded-Measurable-Scalar-Conductivities-in-Three-Dimensions-September-23-2026/build/paper.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:6c2246d27c61a45a1b18c52164bc74ecd19dd7d989ef82442b6e5f594763e5bd","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Nonuniqueness-for-Bounded-Measurable-Scalar-Conductivities-in-Three-Dimensions-September-23-2026/build/paper.tex#L98"},"statement_kind":"corollary","text":"\\label{cor:localized}\nLet $c,C$ be the constants in Theorem~\\ref{thm:main}.\nFor every bounded connected Lipschitz domain $\\Omega\\subset\\R^3$\nand every finite family of pairwise disjoint balls\n$B_1,\\ldots,B_m\\Subset\\Omega$, $m\\geq1$, there are $2^m$\npairwise distinct real scalar conductivities\n$\\gamma_\\varepsilon\\in L^\\infty(\\Omega)$, indexed by\n$\\varepsilon\\in\\{0,1\\}^m$, such that\n\\[\n c\\leq\\gamma_\\varepsilon\\leq C\\quad\\text{almost everywhere},\n \\qquad\n \\gamma_\\varepsilon=1\\quad\\text{on }\n \\Omega\\setminus\\bigcup_{i=1}^m B_i,\n\\]\nand all their full weak Dirichlet-to-Neumann operators from\n$H^{1/2}(\\partial\\Omega)$ to $H^{-1/2}(\\partial\\Omega)$ agree.\nDistinct conductivities differ on a set of positive measure."}
